WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.270
- Family, kindness
(audience clapping)

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:04.610
and a slew of new heartwarming
Hallmark Christmas movies

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.180
to enjoy from the comfort
of your own couch.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.110
My first guests are the current Queens

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.550
of Hallmark Christmas.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.750
First, please welcome Holly
Robinson Peete, everybody

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.750
(audience cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:26.536 --> 00:00:28.170
I can't touch you.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.851
Yo, yo, yo that's (laughing).

00:00:29.851 --> 00:00:31.156
I was like, "Don't touch me."

00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:33.032
- And you'd only just told
me that two seconds ago.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.695
But then what did I do?
- I know, it's so odd though.

00:00:34.695 --> 00:00:35.528
I know.
- We can't help it,

00:00:35.528 --> 00:00:36.361
we're human beings.

00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:37.194
- Claudine will be all over us.

00:00:37.194 --> 00:00:38.230
So I literally was like,

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.610
No. I was like, yeah.
- No, no, I was like.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:44.030
- But, hey everybody,
also we have via Skype,

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:46.508
Candace Cameron Bure and Lacey Chabert.

00:00:46.508 --> 00:00:47.341
What's up, ladies?

00:00:47.341 --> 00:00:52.120
(crowd cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.329
- I can't hug y'all either,
so don't come over here.

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:55.910
(Holly laughing)

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.880
Well, so you have all been making

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.730
Hallmark movies in Canada, right?

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.160
So how was it filming in?
- That's right.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.020
I love Canada.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:03.853
Where are you?

00:01:03.853 --> 00:01:05.220
- We're in Vancouver,

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.480
mostly, I mean, we shoot
- Oh, I love.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.810
in other places in Canada,
but the three of us,

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.280
I think I would say we shoot

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.840
most of our movies in Vancouver,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.090
which for me is like when I was in my 20s

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.010
on 21 Jump Street.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.350
That's where we were.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.290
So every time I go back up there,

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.180
I try to pretend I'm 20
again, which I'm not.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.300
- Oh my God, I don't wanna
be 20 again ever (laughing).

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.430
- Well, I wanna feel 20,

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.290
but I wanna know what
I know in my fifties.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.580
But these ladies are just like,
it's so fun to go up there.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.480
A little different this
time though, right ladies?

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.900
- 'Cause quarantine, yeah.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:36.890
- Yeah, for sure I--
- Yeah. I'm actually

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.143
still in quarantine right now.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.420
- So, I have two more days of quarantine,

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.710
but if I go a little bit stir-crazy.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:46.720
It's actually been great,

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.770
'cause I'm quarantining
with Marilu Henner,

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:51.160
who plays my mom in my mystery movies.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.450
So that part's super fun,

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.030
but it's very rainy and gray here.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.860
And so I've been working
out a lot and there we are.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.810
Yeah, we have a lot of fun together,

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:02.950
but I've been working out a lot

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.860
and there's a Peloton in this house

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.600
that we're staying in and
I got on for a workout

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.770
and had no idea what hit me,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:14.300
but I bawled my eyes
out during this workout.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.270
- Wait, because it was so
hard that you hated it?

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.200
- No, I love working out.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.260
I love working out, but I think
it's just the gray up here

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.620
and missing my family
and being in quarantine,

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.020
you go a little stir-crazy.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.750
And it was like this
flood of emotional relief,

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.710
which was great.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.290
I felt a whole lot better after it.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.270
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.330
That's an awesome release.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.720
What about you, Lacey?

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.080
- Yeah, we've been up here
for about three months.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.480
I did two Christmas movies

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.250
and now I'm onto the
"Crossword Mysteries".

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.550
I'm actually on set right now,

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.760
I'm in a basement (giggles)
talking to you guys.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:45.598
- It's not creepy at all.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.160
(audience laughing)

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.373
- No, it's like, this whole mystery vibe.

00:02:50.724 --> 00:02:52.830
But I'm here with my husband and my sister

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.440
and my four-year-old daughter, Julia.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.590
And so during quarantine

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:58.070
we were baking every recipe imaginable

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.330
and playing cards and hopscotch

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.873
and I mean, I've seen every
cartoon you can imagine.

00:03:03.873 --> 00:03:05.040
And then I broke my toe

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.910
and I was getting ready
to do a dance movie.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.609
So that was slightly unfortunate.

00:03:08.609 --> 00:03:09.587
(Holly laughing)

00:03:09.587 --> 00:03:10.644
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:10.644 --> 00:03:13.160
- (mumbles) I feel so
happy to be back to work

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.510
and I love being in Vancouver.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.200
Everyone here is so wonderful and kind

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.500
and I'm happy to be here.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.090
- I love Canada.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.150
I love, especially the...
- And they really

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.940
have it all together up
there when it comes to,

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.470
you know making it safe for us to shoot,

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.230
which has been pretty cool.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:30.730
I quarantined with my three big sons.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.240
I almost said something I can't say.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.220
- [Host] Yeah(laughing).

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.500
- But my sons and my
husband and my two dogs.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.137
So I brought everybody up.

00:03:38.137 --> 00:03:39.630
- That's actually cool though.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.270
- It was and it was really, it was cool.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.500
And we actually did bond
and then got to break out

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.880
on my birthday and they joined gyms

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.370
and it was really, you
know, it was nice up there.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.203
- Oh wow.

00:03:50.203 --> 00:03:51.390
- And we talked, the three of us talked,

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:55.180
you know, along the way
because we share our stories

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.073
and leading these Hallmark movies

00:03:57.073 --> 00:04:00.670
is such a blessing, the blessing of work

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.260
and the opportunity, but we bonded.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.140
We've known each other
for a long, long time.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.025
All three of us.

00:04:07.025 --> 00:04:09.649
- That's so cool.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.733
♪ Just hear those sleigh bells jingling ♪

00:04:11.733 --> 00:04:14.380
- [Narrator] Your favorite
holiday tradition is back.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.510
Hallmark Channel's Countdown to Christmas.

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:20.490
Get ready for a sleigh full
of holiday movies, 24/7

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:23.530
and all new original
holiday movie premieres

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.956
every Saturday and Sunday night at eight.

00:04:25.956 --> 00:04:28.033
♪ Just hear those sleigh
bells jingling, ring ting ♪

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:31.096
- [Narrator] Join us for the
warmth and share more merry.

00:04:31.096 --> 00:04:34.620
Countdown to Christmas, all season long.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.166
Only on Hallmark Channel,
the heart of Christmas.

00:04:38.166 --> 00:04:39.330
(audience cheering)
(whooshing)

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.380
- Welcome back, y'all.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.500
That's a peek at some of
the latest Christmas movies

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:44.580
Hallmark has in store this season.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.810
And I'm also here with
the ladies of Hallmark,

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:49.140
Holly Robinson Peete, Candace Cameron Bure

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.340
and Lacey Chabert.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.330
Let's talk Hallmark, ladies.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:56.890
How many hallmark Christmas
movies have y'all been in each?

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:58.850
- I've been in nine Christmas movies.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.020
- Nine Christmas movies?

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.360
Oh my gosh.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.910
- How many, Lacey?

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:03.743
- Ten.

00:05:03.743 --> 00:05:04.930
- Oh my gosh.
- Oh ow.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:05.900
- How many, Holly?

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.720
- And I'll round it out with eight.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.440
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.030
That's a lot of movies.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:11.962
Like, What do you--

00:05:11.962 --> 00:05:12.877
- Yay us!

00:05:12.877 --> 00:05:14.650
- I'm just gonna say that's amazing.

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.230
So here's my question

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.252
and I'll start with you, Holly.

00:05:18.252 --> 00:05:19.970
What do you love about doing these movies?

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.740
Is it like, do you love, people
always ask me about my jobs

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.320
and it's, I love
genuinely who I work with.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.350
Like and I think I'm at
an age where I'm like

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.230
I'm really not gonna go to work
unless that's the scenario.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:31.950
Like, is it, do you love the crew

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.910
or it's always kind of a similar crew?

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.990
- I love the crew, I love the content.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.980
I love the fact that
we're making joyful movies

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.150
at a time when people need to see that.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:44.120
I love being able to force
my kids to watch something

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.541
with me in it on Christmas.

00:05:45.541 --> 00:05:46.520
(Show host giggling)

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:49.350
I love to be able to just
be part of this whole

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:52.550
Hallmark magic and the
movies that we're making

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.910
and one of the movies,
"Christmas in Evergreen"

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:59.200
is this awesome, diverse,
mystical town in Vermont.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.120
And I just think we're
doing some great things.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.300
Candace and Lacey are two people

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.630
that I enjoy being part
of this whole brand.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.560
So, I love it.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.020
You know, it's just,
it's a total blessing.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.030
- I love that.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.730
All right, Lacey, I'll go to you next.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:15.927
- Yeah, it's what Holly said.

00:06:15.927 --> 00:06:17.840
You know, I'm happy and proud

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.210
and I feel like it's a real privilege

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.930
to be a part of something
that just brings joy

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.950
into people's living rooms
for a couple of hours.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.280
And I know growing up my family and I,

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.680
we had our favorite Christmas movies

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:29.770
that we'd watch every year.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:31.580
And so when someone tells me that,

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.320
you know a Hallmark movie is one of theirs

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.460
or one that I've been in, like, I just,

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.470
it makes me so happy.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.660
It's an honor.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.180
And I love that I can
watch them with my daughter

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.080
and I just love Christmas.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.110
So it (giggling) only makes sense

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:45.090
that I enjoy making these movies.

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.530
- Me too girl, I love Christmas.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.210
Candace, what about you?

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:52.670
- Holly, I wish my family would
sit down and watch my movies

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.617
like yours do with you,
(show host laughing)

00:06:53.617 --> 00:06:56.901
but they're like, "I'm not
watching another Hallmark movie.

00:06:56.901 --> 00:06:57.734
(Show host laughing)

00:06:57.734 --> 00:06:59.967
"Let alone with you in it, mom, no."

00:07:00.824 --> 00:07:03.320
But I love making these movies so much

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.860
because it brings so much joy to people.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:06.710
Just what they said

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:10.120
like, this has become
people's holiday traditions

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:13.330
and they find so much
comfort in these movies.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:14.970
And I'm so proud to be a part

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.480
of the Hallmark family
and the Hallmark brand.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.890
This will be my 26th movie
with Hallmark channel.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.463
- Oh my God, that's insane
(audience gasping)

00:07:23.463 --> 00:07:25.930
and I'm telling you, my sister
and mother are those women.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:29.610
They literally have seen every single one.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.730
Like, every year they get so excited

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.650
like, "My Hallmark movies
are about to start up,"

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.200
and they're like so excited about it.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.033
It's awesome.

